# F19 reproducer, resolved upstream (bbcf59dc): a matmul inner-dimension mismatch inside grad is a structured error ("shape mismatch") instead of a Rust panic; scripts/run-probes requires the error and forbids a panic.
W = param[8, 8];
x = reshape(range(8), [1, 8]);
h = linear(16, 5, 1);
print("grad", grad(reduce_add(apply(h, matmul(x, W))), W))
